# Local secrets for `wrangler pages dev` (npm run dev:cf).
# Copy to .dev.vars (git-ignored) and fill in. In production set these as
# Cloudflare Pages secrets instead, e.g.:
#   npx wrangler pages secret put ADMIN_PASSWORD
#
# Admin dashboard password. Use a long, random value.
ADMIN_PASSWORD=change-me-to-a-long-random-string

# Recommended: a separate random secret (at least 32 characters) for signing
# admin sessions, e.g. from `openssl rand -base64 48`. Without it the signing
# key is derived from ADMIN_PASSWORD alone.
# SESSION_SECRET=

# Optional: ntfy.sh topic for push notifications when a pin is created.
# ntfy topics are public to anyone who knows the name — treat it like a
# password (long and random) and note that comments are sent in the clear.
# NTFY_TOPIC=

# Optional: an address shown on the landing page ("Try it before you host it").
# Leave unset to hide that section.
# CONTACT_EMAIL=
